# Throwaway build-script variants.
#
# `build_entry.sh` derives REPO_ROOT from its own location, so an A/B build of a *different
# configuration has to be a copy of the script placed in this directory. Those copies are made,
# used once and deleted - but 279's control build left one behind long enough for `git status` to
# offer it, and a build script that is never meant to be committed is exactly the kind of file that
# gets committed by accident. This pattern makes that impossible rather than unlikely.
*_variant.sh
zz_*.sh
